   14. Compliance and Reinstatement.

      All grants in this License are conditioned on compliance with its
      applicable terms. A material breach terminates Your rights under
      this License. Cease the noncompliant activity and fully correct the
      breach. Rights terminated under this section are automatically
      reinstated when You do so before receiving the Producer's first
      written notice of that breach, or within 30 days after receiving
      that first notice, provided You have not previously had rights
      reinstated under this section. Other reinstatement requires the
      written agreement of the licensor entitled to restore those rights.

      This section restores only rights terminated for a material breach
      under this section. It does not automatically restore a patent
      license terminated because of patent litigation under Section 3;
      that requires separate written permission from the relevant patent
      licensor. Reinstatement does not authorize earlier unauthorized
      conduct or erase liability for it. This section does not terminate
      a compliant recipient's independent rights or rights under another
      applicable license.

